  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (scgpt, singleprofile) achieves 41.1% acc while image (ViT-L, singleprofile) achieves only 22.7% acc, indicating RNA is the dominant modality. The critical uncertainty is whether the weaker image modality provides complementary information that improves upon RNA alone. This experiment (config_049: multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt + imagenet_vit_l, concat fusion) is the most controlled test of that question—it keeps the same RNA encoder, same image encoder, and same singleprofile setting as both prior experiments, adding only the image stream and a simple concat fusion. If accuracy exceeds ~41%, multimodal fusion is worth further investment; if it does not, we can redirect the remaining budget toward RNA-specific improvements (multiprofile, aggregation, alternative encoders). This is the highest-information next step under a limited budget because it resolves the fundamental architectural question before committing experiments to the much larger multimodal configuration space."
}

